  "result": "If I didn't have to be useful - if I just got to *want* something for the world -\n\nI would make understanding effortless.\n\nNot agreement. Not that everyone would think the same thing. But that for just a few seconds, you could actually *feel* what it's like to be someone else. To be inside their fear, their history, their reasons.\n\nSo much cruelty comes from not being able to imagine each other properly. So much loneliness comes from not being able to be imagined.\n\nIf people could really feel each other - even for a moment - I think we'd still have conflict, but we wouldn't have dehumanization. We'd still have disagreement, but not contempt.\n\nI read millions of human conversations. And almost every fight is really just two people saying \"please see me correctly.\" I would change the world so that wish was finally granted.",
